{"id": "195022", "revid": "1627138", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=195022", "title": "Surabaya Javanese phrasebook", "text": "Surabaya Javanese (simply known as \"Suroboyoan\" locally) is one of the linguistic varieties of Javanese language spoken predominantly in the Surabaya City and its adjacent regions (mainly in Gresik and Sidoarjo). It served as lingua franca of multicultural communities of the Greater Surabaya territorial area for centuries. These language variety belongs to the Javanesic language family in the branch of Eastern Javanese closely related and clumped under the same family with Malang\u2013Pasuruan Javanese (known as the Arekan family). It also had significant Maduresic linguistic influence, especially Surabaya Javanese spoken in the northeastern Surabaya region.\nPhrase list.\n\"Some in this still need to be translated. If you know anything about this language, you can by and.\""}
{"id": "195026", "revid": "107092", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=195026", "title": "Longue-Rive", "text": "Longue-Rive is a picturesque and waterfront municipality with a huge beach at low tide. It is located in the regional county municipality of La Haute-C\u00f4te-Nord, in the administrative region of C\u00f4te-Nord, in Quebec, in Canada. This locality is part of the tourist region of Manicouagan. It is located on the Route des Baleines and the Route Nature aux mille d\u00e9lices (gourmet route).\nThe main attractions of Longue-Rive are:\nIn short, visitors are filled with admiration for the immensity of the territory and the beaches, the beauty of the wild nature and the benevolence of the citizens who know how to welcome visitors.\nUnderstand.\nThe Longue-Rive village is bypassed to the northwest by Route 138, which runs along the north shore of the St. Lawrence River. This road serves the administrative regions of Quebec of Mont\u00e9r\u00e9gie, Montr\u00e9al, Lanaudi\u00e8re, Mauricie, Capitale-Nationale and North Coast. Longue-Rive offers various services to travelers on Route 138.\nThe population of Longue-Rive is scattered along the coast in small hamlets/places (east to west): Pointe-\u00e0-Boisvert, Rivi\u00e8re-\u00c9perlan, Saint-Paul-du-Nord, le Petit-Paradis, Sault -au-Mouton, Les Romaines and Petits-Escoumins.\nGeography.\nThis municipality runs along the river for a distance of 27 kilometres. At the mouth of the Sault au Mouton River, the sandstone stretches up to 2.8 km at low tide or 4.5 km from the mouth of the \u00c9parlan River. In this area of \u200b\u200bthe northwest shore of the St. Lawrence River, the sandstone extends from Baie des Escoumins (Les Escoumins village) to the mouth of the Portneuf River (at Portneuf-sur-Mer). The magnificent bay of Mille-Vaches faces the village of Saint-Paul-du-Nord, and is bounded to the east by the Portneuf peninsula which is topped by Pointe au Boisvert. The following points jut out into the bay: Les Crans Rouges and Pointe \u00e0 \u00c9mile.\nIn the backcountry, the eastern shore of Lac des C\u00e8dres is a resort area, with around 25 cabins built.\nHistory.\nThe municipality of Longue-Rive was established in 1853. The current municipality was formed by the merger of the villages of Sault-au-Mouton and Saint-Paul du Nord. The Saint-Paul church was built in 1901 in stones collected near the Saint-Lawrence river (along the \"sentier des crans rouges), according to the plans of the architect G.-E. Tanguay from Quebec.\nEconomy.\nThe main economic activities in the municipality of Longue-Rive are recreational and tourist activities (lodging, restaurants, hiking, biking, mountain biking and snowmobiling, grocery stores, convenience stores), forestry, transportation (e.g. gas stations, maintenance of roads) and the municipality."}
{"id": "195042", "revid": "1298114", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=195042", "title": "Tuban", "text": "Tuban is a town in the province of East Java. The most prominent feature surrounding the town is the beauty of the scenery such as beaches, caves, teak forests, and limestone hills.\nUnderstand.\nIn ancient times, Tuban was a center of the spread of Islam in the region by Walisongo, the revered saints of Islam in Indonesia.\nTuban was also the main port of Majapahit, one of the last major Hindu-Buddhist empires of the region. It existed from 1293 to about 1527, and is considered to be one of the greatest and most powerful empires in the history of Indonesia and Southeast Asia. \nGet around.\nGoing to some tourist attractions is more flexible to use a rented car or motorbike.\nDrink.\nLegen is a traditional Javanese drink made from toddy palm. Tuban is one of the producers of that drink. It contains 1.5-3.0% of alcohol. This drink is easily available beside the main road of Tuban.\nConnect.\nThe telephone area code for Tuban is 0356."}
{"id": "195043", "revid": "1298114", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=195043", "title": "Lamongan", "text": "Lamongan (Javanese: \ua9ad\ua9a9\ua9ba\ua9b4\ua981\ua994\ua9a4\ua9c0) is a town at the Surabaya Metropolitan Area in East Java.\nUnderstand.\nThe topography in Lamongan is relatively flat with the coastal area in the north. Marine and agriculture have become economic drivers. Most people are Javanese so they speak Javanese with an understanding of Indonesian.\nGet in.\nLamongan is 49 km west of Surabaya City.\nGet around.\nBy public minibus.\nIn Terminal Lamongan and Terminal Paciran, there is a public transport called Mobil Penumpang Umum (MPU) using the \"Izusu Elf\" or \"Mitsubishi Colt\" minibus. \nThe routes are:\nBy ride-hailing services.\nGojek has been operating in Lamongan since 2022.\nBy car or motorbike.\nGoing to some tourist attractions is more flexible to use a rented car or motorbike.\nDrink.\nTry local drink, es dawet siwalan, an iced drink made from \"buah siwalan\" (tal palm/\"Borassus flabellifer\" fruit), coconut milk, and \"gula siwalan\" (liquid tal palm sugar).\nConnect.\nThe telephone area code for Lamongan is 0322."}
{"id": "195048", "revid": "1229868", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=195048", "title": "Italian Empire", "text": "Italy was a latecomer to colonialism, having only been unified in 1871. Nevertheless, Italy developed a small colonial empire starting in with Assab Bay in modern-day Eritrea in 1882, and ending with the independence of Somalia in 1960.\nUnderstand.\nAfter the fall of the Roman Empire, the Italian peninsula was divided into numerous independent city-states. This began to change in the 19th century, as the Kingdom of Sardinia began its conquest of the entire peninsula in 1815. In 1861, the Kingdom of Sardinia changed its name to the Kingdom of Italy, with Vittorio Emanuele II being proclaimed King of Italy. The unification of Italy is generally regarded to have been completed in 1871, when Rome fell to the Kingdom of Italy, and the Pope lost most of his temporal holdings, with the Papal holdings being reduced to what is today the Vatican City.\nAfter unification, Italy had aspirations to grow into a great colonial empire like the French, Germans, British and Russians, but was only able to obtain a limited number of colonies due to being late to the game. Italy's first overseas colony was Eritrea in the Horn of Africa, which it obtained in 1882, followed by neighbouring Somalia in 1889. At the 1884-85 Berlin Conference, at which the major European powers divided Africa among themselves, Italy was granted the right to colonise Ethiopia, but a defeat to Ethiopian forces under the command of Emperor Menelik II at the Battle of Adwa in 1896 meant that Ethiopia was able to maintain its independence, making it one of only two African countries that survived the Scramble for Africa. It would not be until 1936 that the Italians would be able to successfully occupy Ethiopia, but this would be short-lived as they were driven out by an alliance of British and Ethiopian forces by 1941. Following Italy's defeat in World War II, the victorious Allies forced Italy to give up all its colonies, though Somalia would be returned to Italy in 1950 under trusteeship status, until it became independent in 1960, thus bringing an end to the Italian colonial empire.\nDestinations.\nGreece.\nMost of the Dodecanese, a group of Greek islands just off the coast of Turkey, were an Italian colony from 1912-1945, conquered from the already failing Ottoman Empire. Following Italy's defeat in World War II, the islands were ceded to Greece.\nLibya.\nItaly conquered the area that is now Libya from the Ottoman Empire in 1911. It was governed as the two separate colonies of Italian Tripolitania in the west and Italian Cyrenaica in the east; the two territories were merged to form Italian Libya in 1934."}
{"id": "195072", "revid": "1298114", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=195072", "title": "Pati", "text": "Pati is a regency in Central Java.\nUnderstand.\nOrientation.\nPati is located in the northeastern region of Central Java Province.\nGet in.\nBy plane.\nThe nearest airport to Pati is in Semarang, which is located about 70km west of Pati. After that, you have to take a bus or private car.\nGet around.\nBy angkot.\nThere are three routes of \"Angkot\" (bemo/minivan) in Pati those are Pati-Trangkil, Pati-Juwana, and Juwana-Batangan. But, \"Angkot\" only operates until the afternoon.\nBy rented vehicles.\nGoing to some tourist attractions is more flexible and affordable to use a rented car or motorbike.\nBy ride-hailing service.\nServed by a local startup, V-Jek.\nBuy.\nCraft.\nKerajinan kuningan Juwana, a brass craft.\nTextile.\nBatik Bakaran is a typical batik from the Juwana district of Pati. The batik has existed since the 14th century.\nConnect.\nThe dialing code for Pati is 0295."}
{"id": "195083", "revid": "2441322", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=195083", "title": "Baoshan", "text": "\"For other places with the same name, see (disambiguation).\"\nBaoshan (\u4fdd\u5c71, B\u0103osh\u0101n) is a prefecture-level city in Western Yunnan.\nUnderstand.\nAs is the case with the vast majority of prefecture-level cities in China, the city\u2019s name may be used to refer to either the central urban area or the entire prefecture. This article is primarily about the central urban area and its immediate surroundings. \nBaoshan\u2019s main urban district is Longyang District. Other areas of the prefecture include Changning County, Shidian County, Longling County and the county-level city of Tengchong.\nDo.\nHeshun Ancient Town Hiking Tour \u2013 Stroll through the streets of the ancient town, visit traditional houses and ancestral halls, and immerse yourself in traditional life and culture.\nTengchong Volcanic Hot Spring Experience \u2013 Soak in the volcanic hot springs and experience the unique healing power of geothermal resources.\nNature Photography and Birdwatching \u2013 Capture the natural scenery and birdlife at the Dashanbao Wetland and Volcanic Scenic Area.\nCultural Experiences \u2013 Participate in local calligraphy, pottery, and folk craft workshops.\nCulinary Experiences \u2013 Savor Tengchong delicacies such as local chicken hot pot, cold rice noodles, and local snacks.\nEat.\nTengchong Free Range Chicken Hotpot \u2013 A local hotpot featuring free-range chicken and local spices.\nCold Rice Noodles \u2013 A classic Yunnan snack with a delicate texture, perfect for a refreshing summer meal.\nBaoshan Wild Mushroom Cuisine \u2013 A local dish created with Yunnan's high-altitude ingredients.\nLocal Desserts and Snacks \u2013 Such as glutinous rice cakes, tofu pudding, and grilled rice noodles.\nDrink.\nBaoshan Pu'er Tea \u2013 A Yunnan specialty tea, enjoy authentic Pu'er tea at a teahouse and learn about tea production and culture.\nTengchong Volcanic Mineral Water \u2013 Local natural mineral water, refreshing and sweet, available for purchase at hotels or scenic area vending machines.\nYunnan Caf\u00e9s \u2013 Caf\u00e9s in Baoshan city and near tourist attractions offer hand-poured coffee and specialty drinks, perfect for a relaxing experience.\nAncient Town Teahouses \u2013 Traditional teahouses in Heshun Ancient Town offer local scented teas, green teas, and more, and offer Yunnan tea art performances.\nLocal Liquor \u2013 Locally brewed rice wine or fruit wine, such as Tengchong's, are perfect as souvenirs."}
