{"id": "196965", "revid": "2386027", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=196965", "title": "Esan phrasebook", "text": "Esan is a language spoken mainly in Edo State of Nigeria. It is a tonal language in the Edoid family, with several dialects.\nPronunciation guide.\nVowels.\na\ne\n\u1eb9\ni\no\n\u1ecd\nu\nConsonants.\nbh\ngb\ngh\nkh\nkp\nsh\nch\nPhrase list.\nBasics.\nparts of the body.\nEar. (\"Eh\u1ecd\")\narmpit. (\"Elihele\")\nfingers. (\"\u00cckpiab\u1ecd\")\nface. (\"\u1eb8\u0300lo\")\nhand. (\"Ob\u1ecd\")\ntongue. (\"Olanm\u1eb9 (Ukpolanm\u1eb9)\")\nstomach. (\"\u1eb8k\u1eb9k\u1eb9 (\u1eb8kp\u1eb9k\u1eb9)\")"}
